    <heading level="1">Section 3.1 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Plot Points in a Rectangular Coordinate System</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, plot each point in a rectangular coordinate system and identify the quadrant in which the point is located.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left( {-4,2} \right)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {-1,-2} \right)$$ ⓒ $$\left( {3,-5} \right)$$ ⓓ $$\left( {-3,0} \right)$$ ⓔ $$\left( {\frac{5}{3},2} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>1.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left( {-2,-3} \right)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {3,-3} \right)$$ ⓒ $$\left( {-4,1} \right)$$ ⓓ $$\left( {4,-1} \right)$$ ⓔ $$\left( {\frac{3}{2},1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="3" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left( {3,-1} \right)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {-3,1} \right)$$ ⓒ $$\left( {-2, \text{0} } \right)$$ ⓓ $$\left( {-4,-3} \right)$$ ⓔ $$\left( {1,\frac{14}{5}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>3.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="4" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\left( {-1,1} \right)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {-2,-1} \right)$$ ⓒ $$\left( {2,0} \right)$$ ⓓ $$\left( {1,-4} \right)$$ ⓔ $$\left( {3,\frac{7}{2}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, for each ordered pair, decide</paragraph>
    <paragraph>ⓐ is the ordered pair a solution to the equation? ⓑ is the point on the line?</paragraph>
    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = x + 2;$$ A: $$\left( {0,2} \right);$$ B: $$\left( {1,2} \right);$$ C: $$\left( {-1,1} \right);$$ D: $$\left( {-3,-1} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ A: yes, B: no, C: yes, D: yes ⓑ A: yes, B: no, C: yes, D: yes</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="6" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = x - 4;$$ A: $$\left( {0,-4} \right);$$ B: $$\left( {3,-1} \right);$$ C: $$\left( {2,2} \right);$$ D: $$\left( {1,-5} \right).$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="7" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = \frac{1}{2}x - 3;$$ A: $$\left( {0,-3} \right);$$ B: $$\left( {2,-2} \right);$$ C: $$\left( {-2,-4} \right);$$ D: $$\left( {4,1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ A: yes, B: yes, C: yes, D: no ⓑ A: yes, B: yes, C: yes, D: no</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
